/T (We selected this project to develop a practical application that demonstrates the use of Java programming and Object-Oriented Programming \(OOP\) concepts in a real-world system. A Library Management System provides an appropriate environment to apply concepts such as encapsulation, abstraction, inheritance, and polymorphism while also working with GUI development, file handling, CRUD operations, and exception handling.)
/E (We selected this project to develop a practical application that demonstrates the use of Java programming and Object-Oriented Programming \(OOP\) concepts in a real-world system. A Library Management System provides an appropriate environment to apply concepts such as encapsulation, abstraction, inheritance, and polymorphism while also working with GUI development, file handling, CRUD operations, and exception handling.)
