/T (The Library Management System is organized into several components that work together to provide the complete functionality of the application. The Main class starts the application and opens the MainFrame, which acts as the main GUI window. The GUI communicates with the system's model and file-handling components to manage books, members, and reports. The FileManager handles the storage and modification of data in books.txt and members.txt, while the generated library report is stored in library_report.txt.)
/E (The Library Management System is organized into several components that work together to provide the complete functionality of the application. The Main class starts the application and opens the MainFrame, which acts as the main GUI window. The GUI communicates with the system's model and file-handling components to manage books, members, and reports. The FileManager handles the storage and modification of data in books.txt and members.txt, while the generated library report is stored in library_report.txt.)
