739 0 obj
<<
/Title (The project aims to apply fundamental Java programming and Object-Oriented Programming \(OOP\) concepts in a practical software project. It focuses on implementing encapsulation, abstraction, inheritance, and polymorphism, along with file handling, input validation, exception handling, and persistent data storage. Another goal is to provide proper error and success messages so that users can interact with the system easily and correctly.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 727 0 R
>>
endobj
740 0 obj
<<
/Title (We selected this project to develop a practical application that demonstrates the use of Java programming and Object-Oriented Programming \(OOP\) concepts in a real-world system. A Library Management System provides an appropriate environment to apply concepts such as encapsulation, abstraction, inheritance, and polymorphism while also working with GUI development, file handling, CRUD operations, and exception handling.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 729 0 R
>>
endobj
741 0 obj
<<
/Title (Managing books and member information manually can make it difficult to maintain, update, and retrieve library records efficiently. This project was developed to provide a simple computerized system where book and member information can be stored, viewed, updated, and deleted in an organized manner. The system also provides validation, error handling, and report generation to make common library management tasks more structured and convenient.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 730 0 R
>>
endobj
