791 0 obj
<<
/Title (The project applies the major Object-Oriented Programming concepts of Encapsulation, Abstraction, Inheritance, and Polymorphism. Encapsulation is implemented through private fields and getter/setter methods in the model classes. Abstraction is implemented through the abstract Person class. Inheritance is demonstrated by the Member class extending Person. Polymorphism is implemented through the overriding of the displayInfo\(\) method in the Member class. The project also uses Java Swing for GUI development, file handling for persistent data storage, and exception handling for managing invalid input and file-related errors.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 787 0 R
>>
endobj
